  "live_records": {
    "q-43486": {
      "dom_id": "step-q43486",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "$\\frac{(\\frac{3}{7})}{(\\frac{1}{4})}=$",
      "worked_solution": "First, remember that a fraction represents a division.  So, a fraction of fractions is a division of two fractions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(\\frac{3}{7})}{(\\frac{1}{4})}=\\frac{3}{7}÷\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall that dividing by $\\frac{1}{4}$ is the same as multiplying by its reciprocal $\\frac{4}{1}.$ We can use this fact to simplify the fraction above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{7}÷\\frac{1}{4} & = \\\\ \\frac{3}{7}\\times \\frac{4}{1} & = \\\\ \\frac{3\\times 4}{7\\times 1} & = \\\\ \\frac{12}{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{(\\frac{3}{7})}{(\\frac{1}{4})}=\\frac{12}{7}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
