    "q-43479": {
      "dom_id": "step-q43479",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "$\\frac{3}{(\\frac{7}{3})}=$",
      "worked_solution": "First, remember that a fraction represents a division:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{(\\frac{7}{3})}=3÷\\frac{7}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall that $3=\\frac{3}{1}$ and dividing by $\\frac{7}{3}$ is the same as multiplying by its reciprocal $\\frac{3}{7}.$ We can use these facts to simplify the fraction above:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3÷\\frac{7}{3} & = \\\\ \\frac{3}{1}\\times \\frac{3}{7} & = \\\\ \\frac{3\\times 3}{1\\times 7} & = \\\\ \\frac{9}{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{(\\frac{7}{3})}=\\frac{9}{7}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
