    "q-43489": {
      "dom_id": "step-q43489",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "$\\frac{(-\\frac{14}{3})}{(-8)}=$",
      "worked_solution": "We can use either of the following two methods.\n\n**Method 1 - The Long Way**\n\nFirst, remember that a fraction represents a division:\n\n$$\n\\frac{(-\\frac{14}{3})}{(-8)}=(-\\frac{14}{3})÷(-8)\n$$\n\nNow, recall that dividing by $-8$ is the same as multiplying by its reciprocal $-\\frac{1}{8}.$ We can use this fact to simplify the fraction above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-\\frac{14}{3})÷(-8) & = \\\\ (-\\frac{14}{3})\\times (-\\frac{1}{8}) & = \\\\ \\frac{14\\times 1}{3\\times 8} & = \\\\ \\frac{14}{24}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify:\n\n$$\n\\frac{14}{24}=\\frac{14÷2}{24÷2}=\\frac{7}{12}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\frac{(-\\frac{14}{3})}{(-8)}=\\frac{7}{12}.\n$$\n\n**Method 2 - The Quick Way**\n\nThe result will have the same numerator as the top fraction, and the denominator is just the product of the two denominators:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(-\\frac{14}{3})}{(-8)} & = \\\\ \\frac{-14}{3\\times (-8)} & = \\\\ \\frac{-14}{-24} & = \\\\ \\frac{-14÷2}{-24÷2} & = \\\\ \\frac{7}{12}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
